y":0.05093537195288863,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":99.7,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.013307736206989496,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":-0.007056513016731103,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.08359669631175412,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":86.1,"_gate_incr_roic":0.03993264422828454,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":30.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.01631353269881408,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":27.9,"_gate_pool_share":-0.07301415841938164,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":10.8,"_gate_rev_durability":0.036213998061483954,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":43.1,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.055503685425503074,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":55.5,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.010900774933274428,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":23.2,"_gate_share_shrink":0.031140465626096514,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":11.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.0028400002,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"IDACORP, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, engages in the generation, transmission, distribution, purchase, and sale of electric energy in the United States. The company operates 17 hydropower generating plants located in southern Idaho and eastern Oregon; and three natural gas-fired plants situated in southern Idaho, as well as interests in a coal-fired and natural gas-fired steam generating plant located in Wyoming; and interests in a coal-fired steam generating plant situated in Nevada. As of December 31, 2025, it had approximately 4,730 pole miles of high-voltage transmission lines; 23 step-up transmission substations located at power plants; 21 transmission substations; 12 switching stations; 31 mixed-use transmission and distribution substations; 188 energized distribution substations; approximately 30,020 linear miles of distribution lines; and a capacity of 1,228 MWh of battery storage. The company provides electric utility services to approximately 664,000 retail customers in southern Idaho and eastern Oregon. It serves commercial and industrial customers, which involved in food processing, electronics and general manufacturing, agriculture, health care, government, education, and information technology. The company also invests in housing and other real estate tax credit investments. IDACORP, Inc. was founded in 1915 and is headquartered in Boise, Idaho.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Lisa A. Grow | CEO, President & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $2.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $834K ranks in the below the sector median among Utilities peers. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["IDACORP, Inc. is a mid-cap utilities business with a $8.6B market cap on $1.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $577M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.1%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 47% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.47421914490846445},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","40 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"IDACORP (IDA) Raised Guidance And Revenue Grew, Is It Still Below Fair Value?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nyse-ida/idacorp/news/idacorp-ida-raised-guidance-and-revenue-grew-is-it-still-bel","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794226937.169,"origin":"ti